# No CDN For Production Assets

## Policy

- **Production** (anything shipped to browsers or enforced at runtime for user-facing responses) must **not** load **executable or author-controlled layout assets** from public third-party CDNs: scripts, ES modules, stylesheets, or webfonts, except where an **existing** legacy path is explicitly documented below and scheduled for removal.
- **Preferred pattern:** `npm` dependencies built into the Vite bundle / Django `staticfiles` (`'self'`), same as Bokeh loaded from `@bokeh/bokehjs` in the SPA bundle.
- **Tests and tooling** may use CDNs when necessary (e.g. Playwright loading Bokeh from jsDelivr because jsdom lacks canvas). Restrict those URLs to **`**/tests/**`**, **`test_*.py`**, **`*.test.js`**, **`*.test.jsx`**, and similar—never to templates, middleware, SPA app source, or service configs that define what end users load.

## What counts as production

- Django **middleware** (CSP headers), views, and templates served to users.
- React/Vite **application source** under `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/` and production **`index.html`** (built output under `static/frontend/`).
- Nginx/site configs that inject or proxy **external** script/style/font URLs to clients.
- **Not** production: unit/integration E2E tests, Cursor rules, `TESTING.md` examples, pipeline fixtures.

## CSP relationship

- Do **not** add new `script-src`, `style-src`, or `font-src` entries for arbitrary CDNs to ship a feature. If an API needs a new host, use **`connect-src`** (or document server-side-only calls) per `react-js-cursor-rule.mdc`, not asset CDNs.
- Tightening CSP by removing unused CDN origins is encouraged when the underlying `@import` / `<link>` is removed.

## Repository scan (inventory)

| Location | CDN / third-party host | Role |
|----------|-------------------------|------|
| `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/main.jsx` → Bootswatch `bootstrap.min.css` | **`https://fonts.googleapis.com`** (and **`fonts.gstatic.com`** for font files) | The Spacelab theme CSS contains **`@import url(https://fonts.googleapis.com/...Open+Sans...)`**. Browsers fetch Google Fonts at runtime in production. CSP in `hpcperfstats/site/hpcperfstats_site/middleware.py` allows these hosts for that reason. |
| `hpcperfstats/site/machine/tests/test_bokeh_job_list_embed_browser_e2e.py` | **`cdn.jsdelivr.net`** (`@bokeh/bokehjs`) | **Test-only** Playwright embed regression; allowed. |
| `test_react_spa_view.py` | (assertions) | Asserts served SPA HTML does **not** contain `cdn.pydata.org` or `cdn.jsdelivr.net`. |

No other production source files were found that embed jsDelivr, unpkg, cdnjs, or Bokeh `cdn.pydata.org` scripts. External **API** URLs in Python (e.g. documentation/search links) are not “asset CDNs” for this rule.

## Remediation direction (Bootswatch + Google Fonts)

To fully align with “no CDN in production,” remove the Bootswatch **`@import`** of Google Fonts by one of: vendoring Open Sans (or a subset) under static and referencing local `@font-face`, using a Bootswatch build variable / forked CSS without the web font path, or post-processing the built CSS in the frontend pipeline. Do that in a dedicated change that also **narrows** `font-src` / `style-src` in `middleware.py` if those hosts become unused, and re-run CSP-related tests.

## Overlap

- Complements **`react-js-cursor-rule.mdc`** (CSP and third-party network use): asset loads from CDNs are **disallowed** in production; API `connect-src` changes remain minimal and explicit.
- Complements **`web-pages-e2e-test-maintenance.mdc`** (Bokeh fixtures may use jsDelivr **only** in the Playwright test module).
